<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: IAWS year pre-tax profit up 14 pct.</title>
<headline>IAWS year pre-tax profit up 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.8		   vs 10.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.531		  vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 2.923		  vs 2.657</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    18.52		  vs 16.18</p>
<p> Turnover		   553.94		 vs 510.59</p>
<p>NOTE - Agribusiness company IAWS Group Plc said on Tuesday that growth came primarily from the organic development of existing business activties.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 21.37		  vs 19.00</p>
<p> Interest		   4.73 charge	  vs 4.27 charge</p>
<p> Tax			  4.04 charge	  vs 3.80 charge</p>
<p> Net taxed		  14.49		  vs 12.39</p>
<p> Attributable	     13.79		  vs 12.05</p>
<p>NOTE - IAWS said it continued its policy of investing in fundamentally strong niche sectors of the food industry in which it has established a competitive advantage. It spent 10.9 million Irish pounds on new investments</p>
<p>Cashflow increased to 17.8 pence per share from 15.3 pence and the return on shareholders' funds was 23 percent.  </p>
<p>Gearing at year-end was 15 percent and borrowings totalled nine million Irish pounds against six million previously.</p>
<p>The group said all its operating units contributed to the improved results.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
